[/TABLE]

[HEADING=3]Interpretation[/HEADING]

[LIST]
[*][B]PHP 8.6 RC5 is fastest per request, but only by 1–3 %.[/B] Versus 8.3 it is +2.7 % guest / +3.1 % member on Host A and +1.9 % / +2.2 % on Host B.
[*][B]PHP 8.3 is consistently the slowest[/B] in the low-concurrency test (~1.5–2.5 % behind).
[*][B]At saturation (100 clients) all versions are within ~1.5 %[/B], which is inside the run-to-run/thermal variance. Host A's c=100 average favours 8.5; Host B's favours 8.2.
[*][B]XenForo 2.3.13 does not gain a major step from PHP 8.4/8.5/8.6.[/B] If you upgrade, do it for support/security, not for a large throughput jump.
[*][B]PHP 8.6 works without [ICODE]php-redis[/ICODE][/B] with the SV add-ons and Credis; all guest/member/admin paths returned HTTP 200 on 8.6 RC5.
[/LIST]

[HEADING=2]Final recommendation[/HEADING]

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Use case[/TH][TH]Recommended stack[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]Guest-heavy community (typical forum)[/TD][TD][B]Stack 3[/B] — Angie page cache + Valkey + PHP 8.5 (8.6 when stable)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Mostly logged-in / low guest cacheability[/TD][TD][B]Stack 1[/B] — plain Angie + PHP 8.5/8.6 + MariaDB[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Bot filtering required[/TD][TD][B]Stack 4[/B] — accept ~90 % cached-page cost and ~18 % dynamic cost[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Avoid[/TD][TD]Stack 2 (Valkey without page cache): more moving parts, lower throughput[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[B]Fastest and most performant overall: Stack 3 with PHP 8.6 RC5 / 8.5[/B] for public forum traffic. [B]Fastest for authenticated traffic: Stack 1 with PHP 8.5/8.6.[/B] The page cache is the only change that produces an order-of-magnitude improvement; PHP major versions are effectively flat for this application.

[HEADING=3]Caveats[/HEADING]

[LIST]
[*]XenForo 2.3.13, single-server loopback tests, self-signed TLS, [ICODE]wrk[/ICODE] synthetic load.
[*]PHP 8.6.0RC5, not a final release.
[*]All versions used the pure-PHP Credis client; phpredis is available for 8.2–8.5 and measured equal in the control, but a different Redis workload could differ.
[*]Anubis requests used [ICODE]User-Agent: setup-bench/1.0[/ICODE] (allowed by policy). A browser first visit would solve one challenge before reaching the cached pages.
[*]Stack passes were sequential; small Stack 1 vs Stack 2 deltas are within thermal/run-order drift. The page-cache and Anubis deltas are far outside that range.
[/LIST]
